{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/RFC-jsonl.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:22:35.763866Z","id":"2e4ca1fae0286ee061e71eb19589371dea750ed52948140388722dadc349a73d","body":{"detail":"docs/RFC-jsonl.md:434-447 says \"One additive change to the canonical schema\" and shows `PathIdentity` with `graph_ref` as the sole `// NEW` field. This change adds `parent: Option<Parent>` to `PathIdentity` (crates/toolpath/src/types.rs:131) and updates the `PathOpen` field table (docs/RFC-jsonl.md:196), the reader pseudo-code (:308, :342) and the writer pseudo-code (:364) for it, but not this section, so the document now contradicts itself about what the struct contains.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":434},"end":{"line":447},"content_hash":"005c3808f49622de5361d70f92fdf9462b02e72b46e6dcaa4a4866406074eb9c"},"suggested_fix":"Add `pub parent: Option<Parent>, // NEW (0.8.0)` to the struct listing and change \"One additive change\" to cover both fields, noting both are optional and omitted when absent.","summary":"The JSONL RFC's Schema Change section still lists graph_ref as the only addition to PathIdentity","tags":["review","review:pr-354-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/RFC-jsonl.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:27:24.925336Z","id":"353ad0bbe1de53b530c77711975f453980fea41badc1d97533324d692c3686b9","body":{"detail":"docs/RFC-jsonl.md:434-447: \"One additive change to the canonical schema\" and a `PathIdentity` listing with `graph_ref: Option<String>, // NEW` and no `parent` field. The same document now describes `parent` elsewhere: :180 (example PathOpen), :196 (field table: \"`PathIdentity.parent` — the step in another path this path continues from\"), :308 and :342 (reader pseudo-code), :364 (writer pseudo-code), :412 (field mapping). crates/toolpath/src/types.rs:131 has `pub parent: Option<Parent>` on `PathIdentity`. `suggestion` fits: a stale section in a doc that is otherwise updated.","kind":"comment","references":"2e4ca1fae0286ee061e71eb19589371dea750ed52948140388722dadc349a73d","summary":"confirmed: the Schema Change section still shows graph_ref as the only addition to PathIdentity","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
